    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d264">

                <pb facs="0393" n="1147" sameAs="frus:frus1917Supp02v02/pg1147"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 656.119/182a</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Ambassador in Great Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Page</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-11-20T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 20, 1917, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>5860. For House: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Question of the requisitioning of Dutch ships is being again urged.
                            Request that you discuss matter with British and French authorities in
                            order to find out their views as to political effect of such action,
                            also the views of the military and naval authorities on this question,
                            having in mind the possibility of Holland turning to Germany if ships
                            are requisitioned.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <p>From Polk for Auchincloss: <quote
                        rend="blockquote">
                        <p>Let me know if there is any particular information or news that you want
                            from here. Public much interested in proposed inter-Allied military
                            conference and the fact that we are to be represented. An important
                            message is being sent House by Page from Rome.</p>
                    </quote>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                        
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
